## What does a technical SEO audit check?

A technical SEO audit checks whether search engines can discover, crawl, interpret and index the pages that matter. The exact scope is agreed before work starts because a small service site and a large ecommerce catalogue create different risks.

Typical checks include:

- **Discovery and crawling:** robots.txt, XML sitemaps, internal links, crawl paths and unwanted URL patterns
- **Indexation controls:** canonical tags, redirects, noindex rules, duplicate URLs and status codes
- **Rendering and mobile use:** important content availability, responsive behaviour, mobile usability and interaction problems
- **Core Web Vitals:** available field data across device types and relevant page-level performance evidence
- **Site architecture:** navigation depth, orphan pages, pagination and internal linking
- **Structured data:** valid markup, eligible types and conflicts between page content and schema
- **Migration or update risks:** changed URLs, redirect coverage and traffic drops where relevant

An audit identifies technical constraints. It does not guarantee a ranking change because rankings also depend on relevance, competition, links and the usefulness of the page.

## What content and AI-search checks are in the same audit?

The £495 technical SEO audit fee also covers a content review and an AI-search visibility check. They sit in the same report. You do not pay twice for the full picture.

- **Content and topical authority:** a gap analysis against your top three organic competitors. It shows which pages have the depth to rank, which are thin and which cannibalise each other, plus a coverage map of where your site has authority and where it has none.
- **AI-search visibility:** whether your site is cited in ChatGPT, Bing Copilot, Google AI Overviews and Perplexity for your five most commercially important queries. Entity coverage and schema quality are reviewed. This gives you a baseline if you later decide to work on AI search.

AI answers vary from one run to the next. The AI section reports what I observed on the day. It is not a promise of inclusion.

