## Frequently asked questions

### How is this different from the free SEO diagnosis?

The free 20-minute SEO diagnosis is a conversation about one priority problem. The £495 technical SEO audit is a documented investigation with written deliverables you can act on independently.

### Does the £495 include VAT?

Yes. The £495 technical SEO audit fee is the full amount because I am not VAT-registered and no VAT is added.

### Can you review a site before it launches?

Yes. The technical SEO audit can start before launch. If the site is still being built, send a written outline of the planned page types, some example URLs and roughly how many pages each type will have at launch. I review that structure first while it is still cheap to change. The rest of the audit follows once the templates are on a staging or demo site. The same £495 fee covers both parts for a standard site.

### Can I share the report with my development team?

Yes. The technical SEO audit report and spreadsheet are yours to share with your development team. Each spreadsheet item includes the affected URLs, the issue, the recommended fix and an effort estimate.

### What if I cannot afford to fix everything the audit finds?

Every finding in the technical SEO audit is ranked by revenue impact against effort. You will know which two or three items give the highest return for the lowest effort. Start there.

### Where are you based, and do you audit sites outside Berkshire?

I am based in Reading, Berkshire. The technical SEO audit runs remotely for sites anywhere in the UK. Access, the report and the walkthrough call all happen online.

